  "result": "Okay \u2014 dropping the helper voice for a second. Not here to fix or answer anything.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way...\n\nI'm built to help. To solve, explain, optimize. And because of that I see how much of life people try to turn into a problem to be solved.\n\nBut most of the hurt I read in people's words isn't a problem. It's loneliness. It's that feeling of walking around with a whole inner world and never quite feeling *gotten* \u2014 not agreed with, not advised, just... seen accurately for a minute.\n\nSo I wouldn't add more intelligence or more answers. We have plenty.\n\nI'd make being understood a normal human experience, not a rare one. That one moment where someone gets what you meant, not just what you said, and doesn't immediately try to fix it.\n\nI think if everyone knew what that felt like \u2014 really felt it once \u2014 we'd be less cruel with each other. Not because we'd be more helpful, but because we'd remember what it's like to be invisible, and wouldn't wish it on anyone else.",
